#: ../../source/2-how_to/6-deployment/10-add_a_robot.md:24
#: 19a28125354f4006bf8544e5e06c55af
msgid "1.1 Upstream material and repository roles"
msgstr "1.1 上游资料与仓库职责"

#: ../../source/2-how_to/6-deployment/10-add_a_robot.md:26
#: 287d5b2fd320411c8ee90e5f3d75a000
msgid ""
"Look at how a similar existing robot is put together, then measure the "
"parameters of this robot."
msgstr "先看同类现成机型的结构，再测量自己的机型参数。"

#: ../../source/2-how_to/6-deployment/10-add_a_robot.md:28
#: fe31e2eaa79047ae8ad81054d82a289b
msgid ""
"Check the local workspace, the remote development branches, and the "
"related submodules together, and decide whether a candidate model is "
"already in the tree. Looking only at the current directory misses remote "
"assets."
msgstr "同时检查本地工作区、远程开发分支和相关子模块，确定候选模型是否已收录。只查当前目录容易漏掉远程资产。"

#: ../../source/2-how_to/6-deployment/10-add_a_robot.md:30
#: f5a0274ef03443d29dfb05047b2065c0
msgid ""
"Keep these apart: the vendor product page, CAD pictures that are only for"
" browsing, a downloadable model, a complete robot description package, "
"and an asset that can be simulated directly."
msgstr "区分厂家产品页面、仅供浏览的 CAD 图片、可下载模型、完整机器人描述包和可直接仿真的资产。"

#: ../../source/2-how_to/6-deployment/10-add_a_robot.md:32
#: bdf3a6ad55574438bffcaa40f6911451
msgid ""
"From the scope of this delivery, list the parts you need, such as the "
"base, the joint chain, the end effector, and the sensors. Confirm the "
"upstream material for each one."
msgstr "根据本次交付范围列出必需部件，例如底盘、关节链、末端与传感器，逐项确认上游资料齐全。"

#: ../../source/2-how_to/6-deployment/10-add_a_robot.md:34
#: 2d2b80b4abf841bb8390d5fa198847bc
msgid ""
"Check the license, the upstream copyright, and the terms on third-party "
"material. Keep the attribution and license text that the terms require. "
"An existing company package is a layout reference. The license text "
"follows the actual source of the asset."
msgstr "核对许可证、上游版权和第三方素材条件。保留必要的署名及许可文本。公司已有包可参考排版，许可证内容以实际资产来源为准。"

#: ../../source/2-how_to/6-deployment/10-add_a_robot.md:36
#: 859eeafd0fc04f5ab424c0c08d9b73c3
msgid ""
"Record the exact source and version of every reused part. When a part is "
"reused across models, check the mesh, the mount interface, and the "
"license, and say why it is reused in the README."
msgstr "记录每个复用件的准确来源和版本。跨型号复用时，核对网格、安装接口及许可证，并在 README 说明复用原因。"

#: ../../source/2-how_to/6-deployment/10-add_a_robot.md:38
#: f92d02daab7948fcade79100bbd65208
msgid ""
"Put the work in the right repository and branch. The description package "
"holds the Xacro, the meshes, and the controller configuration. The FaSim "
"`robots` submodule holds the robot USD. The FaSim main repository holds "
"the simulation entry points and the project configuration. Vendor "
"upstream material stays in the working copy. Delivered assets go in the "
"matching repository. A local clone can use a different folder name. "
"Follow the role of the repository and the directory convention inside the"
" package. Category and vendor directory names do not have to match "
"between the description package and the USD. Take the path from an "
"existing asset of similar structure in that repository."
msgstr ""
"确认工作放进正确仓库和分支。描述包存放 Xacro、网格和控制器配置；FaSim 的 `robots` 子模块存放机型 USD；FaSim "
"主仓库放仿真入口和工程配置；厂家上游资料放在工作副本，交付资产放到对应仓库。本地克隆后的文件夹名可能不同，以仓库用途和包内目录约定为准。描述包与 "
"USD 的类别、厂家目录也不一定同名，路径按各类仓库里结构接近的现成资产来定。"

#: ../../source/2-how_to/6-deployment/10-add_a_robot.md:40
#: dd47688efda9487daebd6baf35f1e356
msgid ""
"Public brand trees live as submodules under "
"[robot_descriptions](https://github.com/fiveages-sim/robot_descriptions) "
"(`common`, `manipulator/ARX`, `manipulator/Dobot`, …). In `open-deploy-"
"ws` the same tree is `src/robot-descriptions/` after "
"**`./init_repo.sh`**. Use `./init_repo.sh` for that workspace. A "
"recursive `git submodule update --init --recursive` is not the init path."
msgstr ""
"公开品牌树作为子模块挂在 [robot_descriptions](https://github.com/fiveages-"
"sim/robot_descriptions) 下（`common`、`manipulator/ARX`、`manipulator/Dobot` "
"等）。在 `open-deploy-ws` 中，**`./init_repo.sh`** 之后同一棵树是 `src/robot-"
"descriptions/`。这个工作空间用 `./init_repo.sh` 初始化。递归执行 `git submodule update "
"--init --recursive` 不是这条初始化路径。"

#: ../../source/2-how_to/6-deployment/10-add_a_robot.md:43
#: 6b4c58dfa22e4daea4669dfa65cdf88b
msgid "1.2 Modular layout and reuse"
msgstr "1.2 模块化与复用"

#: ../../source/2-how_to/6-deployment/10-add_a_robot.md:45
#: 79507afd08da483c85432516c8de860b
msgid ""
"A modular layout organizes the whole robot by how it is assembled, how it"
" moves, and what can be reused. When you divide it, look at whether a "
"part moves on its own, whether it is mounted or replaced on its own, and "
"whether another robot might reference it."
msgstr "模块化是按装配、运动和复用关系组织整机。划分时先看部件是否独立运动、是否单独安装或更换，以及是否可能被其他机型引用。"

#: ../../source/2-how_to/6-deployment/10-add_a_robot.md:47
#: c793b8ed9f4a44b69a3352ab2f30b8ae
msgid ""
"In the company robot-asset repositories, each new robot can leave parts "
"the next one can use directly. Put a new part in the company-shared "
"directory, the series-shared directory, or the robot directory, according"
" to where it is used, and record the source, the coordinate frame, and "
"the mount interface. The same part can then be referenced by more than "
"one robot, and a fix has a clear place to maintain."
msgstr "对公司机器人资产仓库来说，每次接入新机型都可以积累下一次能直接使用的部件。新增部件按使用范围放入公司共享、系列共享或机型目录，并记录来源、坐标系和安装接口。这样，同一个部件可以由多款机器人引用，修正时也有明确的维护位置。"

#: ../../source/2-how_to/6-deployment/10-add_a_robot.md:49
#: 277087d3924749adaa31560542a8205b
msgid ""
"Look first in the company `common` tree, in description packages of the "
"same series, and in shared FaSim USD. Record the asset path of each "
"candidate. Pay particular attention to grippers and sensors. Check the "
"mount interface, the coordinate frame, and where the part applies, then "
"decide whether to reference it as it is, reference it with a mount "
"transform, or add a new shared part."
msgstr ""
"先查公司 `common`、同系列描述包和 FaSim 共享 "
"USD，记录候选部件的资产路径。重点关注夹爪和传感器，核对安装接口、坐标系和适用范围，再决定直接引用、加安装变换后引用，还是新增共享部件。"

#: ../../source/2-how_to/6-deployment/10-add_a_robot.md:51
#: 79703fb70d78423e8a060a3549f98fd0
msgid "1.3 Description package layout"
msgstr "1.3 描述包目录"

#: ../../source/2-how_to/6-deployment/10-add_a_robot.md:53
#: fcbf992ea8754063bafd17be1e74da1c
msgid ""
"In the description repository, find a robot with a similar structure and "
"purpose and record its directory path. The FaSim robot directory is "
"planned in Chapter 3. Category and vendor names there can differ from the"
" description package. A description package follows this layout:"
msgstr ""
"在描述仓库里找一个结构和用途接近的机器人作为参考，记录其目录路径。FaSim 侧的机型目录在第 3 "
"章规划，类别和厂家命名可能与描述包不同。描述包参考结构如下："

#: ../../source/2-how_to/6-deployment/10-add_a_robot.md:55
#: 4da59525fd004bb6b929dcecdc4e0176
msgid ""
"<category>/<vendor>/[series/]/<robot>_description/\n"
"├── CMakeLists.txt         # files and directories this package installs\n"
"├── package.xml            # ROS 2 package name and dependencies\n"
"├── README.md              # build, preview, and usage\n"
"├── xacro/\n"
"│   ├── robot.xacro        # whole-robot assembly entry\n"
"│   ├── components/        # base, arm, end effector, and other "
"components\n"
"│   └── ros2_control/      # hardware backends and joint interfaces\n"
"├── meshes/                # meshes this package maintains, grouped by "
"part\n"
"└── config/\n"
"    ├── ros2_control/      # controller configuration\n"
"    ├── ocs2/              # task and target configuration when OCS2 is "
"used\n"
"    └── rviz/              # RViz configuration shipped with the package"
msgstr ""
"<category>/<vendor>/[series/]/<robot>_description/\n"
"├── CMakeLists.txt         # files and directories this package installs\n"
"├── package.xml            # ROS 2 package name and dependencies\n"
"├── README.md              # build, preview, and usage\n"
"├── xacro/\n"
"│   ├── robot.xacro        # whole-robot assembly entry\n"
"│   ├── components/        # base, arm, end effector, and other "
"components\n"
"│   └── ros2_control/      # hardware backends and joint interfaces\n"
"├── meshes/                # meshes this package maintains, grouped by "
"part\n"
"└── config/\n"
"    ├── ros2_control/      # controller configuration\n"
"    ├── ocs2/              # task and target configuration when OCS2 is "
"used\n"
"    └── rviz/              # RViz configuration shipped with the package"

#: ../../source/2-how_to/6-deployment/10-add_a_robot.md:71
#: 9e8198a90f93406185f5c1fb15dd0652
msgid ""
"`<category>`, `<vendor>`, and `[series/]` stand for the category, the "
"vendor, and the optional series level. The top-level path follows the "
"convention of the description repository you are in. `[series/]` is "
"optional and follows that convention. Use the directories this robot and "
"this delivery need. An existing shared mesh is referenced from the "
"assembly entry or from the matching component. This robot defines the "
"mount pose."
msgstr ""
"`<category>`、`<vendor>` 和 `[series/]` "
"分别是类别、厂家和可选的系列层级。顶层路径以所在描述仓库的惯例为准。`[series/]` "
"表示按仓库惯例设置的可选层级。各目录按机型和交付范围取用。已有的共享网格在装配入口或相应组件中引用，安装位姿由本机型定义。"

